191983788561324_n.jpg?_nc_cat=109&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=ijeDQTNdHewQ7kNvwHddGwG&_nc_oc=AdrGqwcdHRKCOm9spUY1usc24l-wUCDjnpMWrSD2dl5sd3UeqFMOIOjfMzdDOLp0rQJMqbvvexcyp7lRWAdZd_z5&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-3.fna&_nc_gid=aP4v6XI7INEssEQNllsYrA&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af69HUIByC3Vviid5u011sEQ6J_wdGmq8bZNymWdqkEAzg&oe=6A37F373\",\r\n\t  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-3.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/124624874_111203954130838_2354619861861359650_n.jpg?_nc_cat=108&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=MCs-K7OakPMQ7kNvwF8BVfZ&_nc_oc=AdrXe2Ony9hoHpvqU98WuoSvNLQObOmDAHQTYAq9FmFVVz2prUP3Bgq5MevtmSJGwtp-8-lKEPvJSUBde5m2euf_&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-3.fna&_nc_gid=uew3F8vmRpEyaOal2d5BOA&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af7fgTvHsCpLBrOdE_D2WH75VoLXAJGHiDi4WWBiK84xxQ&oe=6A38091B\",\r\n\t  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/124643331_111203980797502_2654554848403633280_n.jpg?_nc_cat=111&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=5YToLg8Cay0Q7kNvwE8IHQE&_nc_oc=AdrB9aQrq-9WrRXUSaYsChJUx3WWJL3EWEnU8YtHM3KUWkNP5O3RpOOEbuVqN95gYgZcsm2gpLZpzhAHQ6BxdPvm&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-1.fna&_nc_gid=Ac9ebWCX3b3v4UrC47uW7w&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af7fZ-HDpK3S9HNf3OIpdMSGWKgmAAEocdlxlGbloJSRRg&oe=6A3822AE\"\r\n\t],\r\n      content: `● في غلط شائع أنه بس الشجر والنباتات بتقدر تعمل عملية التركيب الضوئي وانه غابات الأمازون هي المصدر الأساسي لإنتاج الاكسجين بس الواقع غير هيك\r\n● بقدر العلماء أنه 50-80٪ من إنتاج الأكسجين على الأرض بيجي من المحيط.\r\nمعظم هذا الإنتاج من العوالق المحيطية زي النباتات الطافية والطحالب وبعض البكتيريا يلي بتقدر تعمل تمثيل ضوئي.\r\nنوع معين من البكتيريا اسمه Prochlorococcus وهو أصغر كائن حي قادر على علمية التمثيل الضوئي على الأرض بس هاي البكتيريا الصغيرة بتنتج تقريبًا 20٪ من الأكسجين في محيطنا الحيوي (اكمل القراءة وستجد التعريف) بأكمله وهاي النسبة أعلى من كل الغابات الاستوائية المطيرة على الأرض كلها.\r\n● بس هاد بعنيش أنه العالم بخير وكلشي صبابا واحنا عايشين بكوكب زمردة ومنقدر نعيش بدون أشجار\r\n البحار عم تتلوث ونسبة كبيرة من الحياة البحرية عم تموت والأشجار عم تنقطع وهاد الاشيا بتعمل زيادة فغازات الدفيئة وثقب الاوزون عم يزيد ويكبر بسبب قلة الاكسجين وبالتالي هاي العوامل بتؤدي للاحتباس الحراري يلي عم يصير والتغيرات المناخية\r\n***تعريف صغير للمحيط الحيوي:\r\nهو الحيز يلي موجود فيه الحياة وبمتد من أكبر عمق موجود فيه  الحياة في البحار لحد أعلى ارتفاع موجود عليه الحياة في الجبال.\r\nومكوناته:\r\n1) بشمل كل الكائنات الحية\r\n2) أجزاء من القشرة الأرضية\r\n3) الطبقات السفلى من الغلاف الجوي\r\n4) أعماق البحار ( الغلاف المائي)`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2020-11-09\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n\r\n      ],\r\n      content: `I tried to swim to the side\r\nBut my feet got caught in the middle\r\nAnd I thought I'd see the light\r\nBut oh, no\r\nI was just stuck on the puzzle`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2020-11-08\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n        \"https://scontent.ftlv20-3.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/124478225_110743917510175_9023232249619987809_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=w2LpX_wNdwYQ7kNvwHKRYBY&_nc_oc=Adq1sFLqqb3PylJvnSD8kvlw99gfWm02rnAaASUu358EglQvOnamWD3l2VZb3Bk4TwEzdROYN1UqlMSnnGuDeSSl&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-3.fna&_nc_gid=iDKJJ6CSIYRw0Lx_6lQkyw&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af7kGu-0p0hQne7oLo3o7cgEXWAHR4j92zbCzJHeKAz1zw&oe=6A38027B\"\r\n      ],\r\n      content: `This is the most detailed image of the inner cellular life ever taken.\r\nThere are more than 100 trillion cells in the human body`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2020-11-8\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n\t  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/124801001_110652034186030_6765917709715882898_n.jpg?_nc_cat=102&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=uFIhETcSEv0Q7kNvwG25nyE&_nc_oc=AdrRhcM6cpj-wBpudxyc6nD-uzGBBmdxwB2YibUzk377Avc7h7UaHRWi_0BXU44_DtPp4_zBr9sY9KSlOFOBXQE7&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-2.fna&_nc_gid=zI56yz8_hQJGWnDw6-UVEg&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af4jLV7ZzhewAyVW7A9fD3TNEkF1qlFOfMsRJdijbpZDfg&oe=6A37FBF5\",\r\n\t  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-3.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/124367551_110652060852694_3029223177671412611_n.jpg?_nc_cat=109&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=PwA31WwwUMAQ7kNvwGcU9eY&_nc_oc=AdomPdD_3QhIANRFBYxkaWCgwAZrh0FSUKJObBqe6EshNJv4jccADotDy2mQHxtRpUcCTkOXn0kg975kaPdnoQep&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-3.fna&_nc_gid=Qfl389LUhj_GIk0nvO6_Bw&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af4V4y3TlaOOLSH5jeFBNU2gX141ibRfUQhng1CfE2VdiA&oe=6A381D0F\",\r\n\t  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/videos/mus.mp4\"\r\n\t],\r\n      content: `أغلبنا سمع كلمة بوتوكس فشي مرحلة فحياته وأول ما نسمع هاي الكلمة منربطها دغري بعمليات التجميل بس البوتوكس مش بس بيستخدم بعمليات التجميل في استعمالات ثانية كثيرة بس قبل لنحكي عنها بدنا نعرف شو هو البوتوكس\r\n● البوتوكس هو مادّة بروتينيّة بتتميّز بأنّها بتعيق عمل الاستيل خولين يلي هو واحد من النواقل عصبية يلي بعطي إشارة من الخلايا العصبية للخلايا العضلية وبحفزها على الانقباض أو التقلص (الشرح بالصور والفيديو تحت) فلما منحقن البوتوكس فالعضلات وبعيق افراز الاستيل خولين للسينابسا أو بالعربي التشابك العصبي وبالتالي بمنع أو بقلل تقلّص العضلة.\r\n●طيب بعد ما عرفنا شو هو البوتوكس شو هي الاستعمالات تاعته؟\r\nهاي بعض الاستعمالات اله:-\r\n1) الاستخدام الأكثر شيوعاً فعالم التجميل غير الجراحي هو علاج التجاعيد فالوجه والرقبة.\r\n2) فمجال المشكلات الجلدية بعالج البوتوكس حالات فرط التعرق فحيث بعمل على إيقاف تأثير الإشارات العصبية للغدد العرقية وبخف افراز العرق.\r\n3) علاج الصداع النصفي المزمن  Migraine\r\n4) الانقباض المتكرر لعضلات الرقبة (cervical Dystonia)، وهي حالة مرضية بصير فيها انقباض لاإرادي لعضلات الرقبة، ويلي بسبب التواءها بشكل مفاجئ لاإرادي ومؤلم، بساعد حقن البوتوكس على إرخاء هاي العضلات وبالتالي علاج هاي المشكلة.\r\n5) تشنج العضلات في بعض الأمراض العصبية زي ضمور المخ، بصير تشنج لعضلات الأطراف (الساقين والذراعين) بحيث بتنجذب لجوا باتجاه جذع الجسم.\r\nبساهم حقن البوتوكس فتقليل عوارض هاي الحالة بطريقة فعالة وعلاج اضطراب الحركة عند مرضى الشلل الدماغي.\r\n6) بيستخدم البوتوكس كمام فطب العيون بحيث بساعد فعلاج حالات الحول وكسل العيون يلي بتصير نتيجة لعدم التكافؤ بين انقباض عضلات العين.`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\t{\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2020-11-4\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/123764521_106858141232086_8099276397729435001_n.jpg?_nc_cat=102&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=PbassEzJCvYQ7kNvwGMChqP&_nc_oc=Adr3amMSNwfC_BfnR-JMDBtaUzNNqhr7zo1l80S8nJrRvXjx1UabRy3W3DZMdJ682KF3YbyVdFdY4K2nbLK9okP_&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-2.fna&_nc_gid=VxKxQHtSaX4OoIZDm5SjhQ&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af5z4DojtU7sNZugx7DDmrDgNxGNde5YCgY0ONXTJSsMqg&oe=6A382A4F\",\r\n  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-3.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/123729310_106858161232084_3177574936308390861_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=ttZXrN3EOF4Q7kNvwH9dh6e&_nc_oc=Ado6An5ADl9xD9S-vGWzebJzgeurFGa6Eqf78jbB8u4meHQ3kEHZqATd5N_vlDJL6LVjLJeWWlia3HHCtkNOSTL7&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-3.fna&_nc_gid=GxXwe-V1AsvZMm-N7LeDOg&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af7hUXXYAQF_uAFF77avVPyIj-QraHdgh_svlx4erH8ZCg&oe=6A38262D\",\r\n  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/123750099_106858197898747_2687431113543152938_n.jpg?_nc_cat=111&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=DIW0Q_qwIkAQ7kNvwGZrZi4&_nc_oc=AdpZ4da2PY6eha3HO37hWm3w43t_4flNj42YKEevNt44U4KsN5yJm7OLggWy5oYAnlUqrIWQd-OKg8tjglPpbLI9&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-1.fna&_nc_gid=yGov38E0zLuBY6XCEqLBsA&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af7qKEIIS8OtdttW8hpZ4kh46nw6HVFLPoseLBgPhoHdCQ&oe=6A3823F1\",\r\n  \"https://scontent.ftlv20-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.6435-9/123505770_106858224565411_7257743013202387148_n.jpg?_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=833d8c&_nc_ohc=WXC8wnoLGcoQ7kNvwHwpMU5&_nc_oc=Adrxk4kMG4pElpfZk27t4vFWdczlqTe3tA5SnS5fVUt9fkQ7gl0DpQUxBkyghnKGyjR-sncw8ozYASL64yw-NLq_&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.ftlv20-1.fna&_nc_gid=GCraZahdaIySr8quMQLkmQ&_nc_ss=7b2a8&oh=00_Af73ZXiO_N-Ves3Rb49Q4rOklSXE3zB8aOwhio6dzXm4yg&oe=6A380729\"\r\n],\r\n      content: `● أكيد معظمنا سمع بمصطلح Déjà Vu بس هل منعرف شو معناه؟ مصطلح Déjà Vu هو كلمة فرنسية معناه شفته من قبل- Already seen أغلبنا مر بهاي الحالة يلي منحس لثواني أنه عشنا أو شفنا هاي اللحظه من قبل وبصيبنا نوع من الحيرة بس بنعرفش التفسير العلمي لإلها في كثير تفسيرات سمعناها زي انه:-\r\n1) هاي الخيال البسيط لدى الإنسان.\r\n2) إنّها جزء مجهول من ذكريات قديمة.\r\n3) أنّه الجنين خلال مراحل الحمل بشوف شريط حياته، وبالتالي يلي بحس فيه هو نتيجة أنه تذكر شو شاف وهو فرحم امه فبحس أنه الموقف مألوف وهاد التفسير الخزعبلاتي الأكثر شيوعًا يلي بحكولنا اياه سيادنا.\r\n4) تناسخ الأرواح.\r\n● طب بلاش لف ودوران شو التفسير العلمي الصحيح لهاي الظاهرة؟\r\nالتفسير العلمي الأكثر دقّة والاكثر منطقيّة لهاي الحالة برجع لعمليّة نقل المعلومات عن طريق الأعصاب للمخ، لما نتعامل مع موقف أو حدث معيّن بتم نقل هاي المعلومات لل medial temporal lobe  يلي هو الجزء من المخ يلي مسؤول عن تخزين الذاكرة فشكل عام جوا هاي المنطقة في اشي اسمه الHippocampus المسؤول عن الذاكرة وتحديدا عن الذاكرة طويلة الأمد والتعرف على الأنماط المعروفة من قبل، بس يصير معك اشي بروح على الذاكرة قصيرة الأمد بعدين بتسجل بالذاكرة طويلة الأمد\r\nفحسب نظرية dual processing theory مرات بصير عدم تزامن فتخزين الذاكرة يعني بتسجل فالاول فالذاكرة طويلة الأمد يعني ذكرى قديمة، بفارق اجزاء من الثانية من ما يسجلها على أنها ذكرى قصيرة الأمد  يعني ذكرى جديدة، فهاد عدم التزامن بخدع مخك وبخليك تفكر أنه انت عشت هاي اللحظه من قبل.\r\nhttps://www.scientificamerican.com/.../can-science.../`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\r\n],\r\n  wednesday: [\r\n\r\n {\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2026-06-10\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n        \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/tomo.jpg\",\r\n        \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/tomo1.jpg\",\r\n\t\t  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/tomo2.png\"\r\n\t\t   ],\r\n      content: `⚠\uFE0F Spoiler Warning ⚠\uFE0F\r\n\r\nThere is a good chance you won't understand what I'm about to say.\r\n\r\nYou may think it's confusing. You may feel like nothing is clear.\r\n\r\nThat's okay.\r\n\r\nWhen the time comes and you experience the story yourself, the pieces will slowly fall into place, and you'll finally see the bigger picture.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat is right? What is wrong?\r\n\r\nSounds like an easy question, haa? but naah!!!\r\n\r\nOne day, Yuichi thought he had four loyal friends by his side. The next, he discovered that one of them had betrayed the group and dragged everyone into a debt bigger than any of them could bear.\r\n\r\nWhy?\r\n\r\nWho did it?\r\n\r\nWas it greed? Jealousy? Revenge? Or something else entirely?\r\n\r\nThe problem is that there is never a simple answer.\r\n\r\nEveryone has a motive. Everyone has secrets. Everyone lies. Yet at the same time, everyone seems to genuinely value their friendship.\r\n\r\nAnd that's where the nightmare begins.\r\n\r\nThe challenges don't stop after the first game. In fact, that is only the beginning. The \"Tomodachi Game\" is much bigger than anyone realizes at first. Every game reveals another secret, another betrayal, another hidden truth. Every answer creates even more questions.\r\n\r\nJust when you think you've figured out who the villain is, the story turns everything upside down.\r\n\r\nAgain.\r\n\r\nAnd again.\r\n\r\nAnd again.\r\n\r\nYou start questioning every character. Every action. Every friendship. Every promise.\r\n\r\nWho was the good guy from the beginning?\r\n\r\nWho was truly innocent?\r\n\r\nWho was the real friend?\r\n\r\nWho was only pretending?\r\n\r\nNo matter how much information you gather, the story keeps showing you a bigger picture hidden behind the one you thought was complete.\r\n\r\nThere are twists everywhere. Events that seemed meaningless suddenly become important. Conversations you forgot about return with a completely different meaning. Things were happening in the background the entire time, and you never even noticed.\r\n\r\nBut perhaps the biggest question isn't who betrayed whom.\r\n\r\nIt's this:\r\n\r\nWhen did all of this really start?\r\n\r\nThe answer is far more shocking than you might expect.\r\n\r\nWho initiated it?\r\n\r\nWho set everything into motion?\r\n\r\nWho was pulling the strings from the shadows?\r\n\r\nWhat we are sure about is that all of its started with:\r\nWhat is right? What is wrong?`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n{\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2025-06-03\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n         \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/stupid3.jpeg\",\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/stupid1.jpeg\",\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/stupid2.jpeg\"\r\n      ],\r\n      content: `What is more dangerous to a person: stupidity or overconfidence?\r\n\r\nThis isn't just a random philosophical question. It's one of those questions that can completely change the way you see the people around you.\r\n\r\nLet's start with stupidity.\r\n\r\nFew things are more frustrating than someone who refuses to understand the simplest things, repeats the same mistakes over and over, and creates problems where none should exist. Stupidity doesn't only affect the person who has it—it drains everyone around them. It wastes time, energy, opportunities, and sometimes causes damage that can't be undone.\r\n\r\nWhat's even more frustrating is that some people aren't just uninformed; they actively resist learning. They reject facts, ignore advice, and continue making the same poor decisions while expecting different results.\r\n\r\nYet despite all of that, stupidity has its limits.\r\n\r\nA stupid person may eventually realize they don't know enough. They may ask for help, seek guidance, or hesitate before making a major decision.\r\n\r\nBut then comes overconfidence.\r\n\r\nAnd this is where things get really interesting.\r\n\r\nImagine someone who is completely wrong, yet speaks as if they possess absolute truth. Someone who never doubts themselves, never listens, never questions their assumptions, and treats every disagreement as a personal attack.\r\n\r\nOverconfidence gives people the ability to walk straight into disaster while believing they're heading toward success.\r\n\r\nStupidity may cause a bad decision.\r\n\r\nOverconfidence may convince hundreds of other people to follow that bad decision.\r\n\r\nStupidity is dangerous because it lacks understanding.\r\n\r\nOverconfidence is dangerous because it lacks self-doubt.\r\n\r\nA stupid person can become a problem.\r\n\r\nAn overconfident person can become a catastrophe.\r\n\r\nBut there is another side to the argument.\r\n\r\nSome would say that overconfidence, at least, comes with ambition, courage, and the willingness to take action. Stupidity, on the other hand, can be the root cause of failure, poor judgment, and unnecessary mistakes from the very beginning. According to this view, most disasters start with ignorance, not confidence.\r\n\r\nSo the question remains:\r\n\r\nWho would you rather avoid?\r\n\r\nA stupid person who doesn't understand what's happening around them?\r\n\r\nOr an overconfident person who believes they can never be wrong?\r\n\r\nWhich one is more dangerous to society?\r\n\r\nWhich one is more frustrating to deal with?\r\n\r\nAnd perhaps the most controversial question of all:\r\n\r\nIs overconfidence simply a more sophisticated form of stupidity?\r\n`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n{\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2025-06-02\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n         \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/emu1.jpeg\",\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/emu.jpeg\",\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/emu3.jpeg\"\r\n      ],\r\n      content: `In 1932, Australia declared war.\r\n\r\nNot against another country.\r\n\r\nBut against birds.\r\n\r\nThis is the story of the Great Emu War — one of the strangest “military operations” in modern history.\r\n\r\nAfter World War I, Australian farmers were struggling. Wheat fields were being destroyed, and tens of thousands of emus — large, fast, flightless birds — migrated into farmland looking for food. The damage was so severe that the government decided to intervene using soldiers armed with machine guns.\r\n\r\nYes, machine guns versus emus.\r\n\r\nAt first, it sounded like a serious military operation. Soldiers arrived, set up positions, and attempted to take down the birds. But the emus had something the army didn’t expect: speed, unpredictability, and surprisingly smart group behavior.\r\n\r\nThey scattered in small groups, making them extremely hard to hit. Even when soldiers opened fire, the birds often escaped with minimal losses. Reports from the time even describe machines breaking down and ammunition being wasted with little success.\r\n\r\nThe result was unexpected and almost unbelievable: the emus kept winning. The military struggled to achieve results, and eventually the operation was called off.\r\n\r\nOfficially, the emus were declared “too efficient” to fight in that way.\r\n\r\nWhat makes this story so fascinating is not just its humor, but what it reveals about human expectations versus nature. A highly organized military force, equipped with advanced weapons for its time, struggled against a population of birds simply trying to survive in their environment.\r\n\r\nToday, the Great Emu War is remembered as a historical curiosity, but also as a reminder that intelligence, adaptation, and survival strategies don’t always come from where we expect them.\r\n\r\nSometimes history isn’t just written by humans.\r\n\r\nSometimes… it’s written by emus.\r\n`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  {\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2026-05-27\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/d1.jpeg\",\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/d2.jpeg\",\r\n       \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/d3.jpeg\"\r\n        ],\r\n      content: `Imagine waking up every day knowing your entire purpose is to lose.\r\n\r\nNot because you’re weak. Not because you failed. But because the world already decided your role long before you were even conscious enough to question it.\r\n\r\nThat’s the world of Go! Go! Loser Ranger! — and that’s the life of Fighter D.\r\n\r\nThirteen years ago, monsters invaded Earth. Humanity was supposed to be on the edge of extinction… until the heroic Ranger squad appeared and crushed them. That’s the story everyone knows. That’s what the world believes.\r\n\r\nBut the truth is very different.\r\n\r\nThe war actually ended in just one year.\r\n\r\nThe monsters didn’t disappear — they were kept alive. Controlled. Recycled into a system where every Sunday, the same “battle” takes place again and again. A staged event called the Sunday Battle, broadcast to the public like entertainment.\r\n\r\nThe heroes win every week. The monsters lose every week. And the audience cheers, never questioning why the story never changes.\r\n\r\nFighter D is one of those monsters.\r\n\r\nAt first, he doesn’t think too deeply about it. Survival is enough. Just play your role, take your defeat, and live to see another Sunday.\r\n\r\nBut over time, something breaks inside him.\r\n\r\nBecause if your life is just a performance… if your pain is scripted… then what does any of it mean?\r\n\r\nSo D changes. He stops accepting the role of the “background monster.” He decides to fight back against the Rangers — the so-called heroes who built this system on lies.\r\n\r\nThat becomes his new purpose: revenge.\r\n\r\nBut even revenge doesn’t stay simple.\r\n\r\nHe finds an organization that claims to be fighting for monsters like him. For freedom. For justice. For ending the Rangers’ control. For a moment, it feels like he finally belongs somewhere — like his struggle has meaning again.\r\n\r\nBut every answer he finds comes with another layer of truth.\r\n\r\nAnd slowly, everything he believed starts to collapse.\r\n\r\nBecause the world isn’t just divided into heroes and villains. It’s divided into roles. Scripts. Masks.\r\n\r\nEven the rebellion might just be another part of the performance.\r\n\r\nAnd then comes the hardest realization of all:\r\n\r\nMaybe he was never a “chosen fighter,” or a “hero of monsters,” or even a “rebellion leader.”\r\n\r\nMaybe he was just created to fill a space in someone else’s story.\r\n\r\nSo now the question changes completely.\r\n\r\nNot “Who is my enemy?”\r\nNot “How do I win?”\r\n\r\nBut:\r\n\r\n“If my whole existence is part of a script… what happens when I stop following it?”\r\n“If my whole life was written for me… what am I even supposed to be?”\r\n\r\nAnd that’s where Fighter D is now.\r\n\r\nNo longer just a monster. No longer just a rebel.\r\n\r\nSomething in between — something unpredictable.\r\n\r\nIf the world insists on treating him like a villain…\r\n\r\nthen maybe becoming the villain is the only way to finally become real.`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n    {\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2026-05-27\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n        \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/banana1.jpeg\",\r\n        \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/banana2.jpeg\"\r\n         ],\r\n      content: `\uD83C\uDF4C Bananas are technically radioactive… and that’s actually a real scientific fact. ☢\uFE0F\uD83D\uDE33\r\n\r\nEvery banana contains potassium, which your body needs to survive.\r\nBut here’s the weird part: a tiny amount of that potassium is a radioactive isotope called Potassium-40.\r\n\r\nSo yes… every time you eat a banana, you’re exposing yourself to a microscopic amount of radiation.\r\nCongratulations, your snack is basically a tiny edible science experiment. \uD83D\uDE02\r\n\r\nScientists even have something called the “Banana Equivalent Dose” \uD83C\uDF4C\r\nIt’s an actual joking measurement used to explain small amounts of radiation to people.\r\nOne banana gives you about 0.1 microsieverts of radiation — which is EXTREMELY tiny.\r\n\r\nFor comparison:\r\n✈\uFE0F A flight gives you WAY more radiation because of cosmic rays.\r\n\uD83D\uDCF1 Your phone? Not radioactive.\r\n\uD83C\uDFE5 A chest X-ray? Around 1,000 bananas worth of radiation.\r\n\r\nAnd before anyone panics:\r\nBananas are completely safe. Your body naturally regulates potassium, so you don’t become a walking nuclear reactor after breakfast \uD83D\uDE2D\r\n\r\nIn fact, you’d need to eat around 10 million bananas at once for the radiation to become dangerous…\r\nand honestly, surviving 10 million bananas would already be impossible. \uD83D\uDC80\uD83C\uDF4C\r\n\r\nSo next time someone says they’re eating healthy, remind them they’re also consuming radioactive fruit. \uD83E\uDD1D`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n\r\n {\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2026-05-20\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/rec1.jpeg\",\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/rec2.jpeg\",\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/rec3.jpeg\",\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/rec4.jpeg\"\r\n],\r\n      content: `Have you ever stood between two mirrors facing each other?\r\nYou see yourself repeated infinitely:\r\nan image inside an image inside another image, stretching forever into the distance.\r\nThat strange effect is actually a perfect example of something called Recursion.\r\nRecursion is the idea that something can contain a smaller version of itself.\r\nAnd once you notice it, you start seeing it everywhere.\r\nA tree branch grows smaller branches, and those branches grow even smaller ones with the same shape.\r\nA coastline seen from space often looks similar when zoomed in closer.\r\nEven stories sometimes use recursion:\r\na story about someone telling a story about someone else telling a story.\r\nNature seems obsessed with repeating patterns.\r\nWhat makes recursion fascinating is that complexity can emerge from very simple rules repeated again and again.\r\nNow here’s where programming enters the picture.\r\nProgrammers discovered that problems can also be solved this way.\r\nInstead of solving one huge problem directly, a computer can break it into smaller versions of the same problem until it becomes simple enough to handle.\r\nImagine searching through thousands of folders on your computer.\r\nEach folder may contain smaller folders, and each of those contains more folders.\r\nA recursive program handles this naturally:\r\n“Open a folder, then repeat the same process inside every smaller folder.”\r\nThe same idea powers:\r\n* search engines,\r\n* artificial intelligence,\r\n* fractal graphics,\r\n* game systems,\r\n* and many modern algorithms.\r\nOne of the most interesting examples is something called a fractal.\r\nA fractal is a shape where every tiny part resembles the whole shape itself.\r\nSome fractals can become infinitely detailed no matter how much you zoom in.\r\nWhat’s shocking is that many natural objects behave similarly:\r\nclouds, mountains, lightning, rivers, even broccoli.\r\nAll from repetition.\r\nRecursion teaches a surprisingly deep idea:\r\nsometimes enormous complexity is not created by complicated rules…\r\nbut by simple patterns repeating themselves endlessly.`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n      {\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2026-05-13\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n\t  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/memo1.jpeg\",\r\n\t  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/memo2.jpeg\",\r\n\t  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/memo3.jpeg\"\r\n\t],\r\n      content: `Can memories actually be transferred between living beings?\r\nIt sounds like science fiction, but several real experiments pushed scientists to seriously explore the idea.\r\n\r\nThe Worm Experiments, in the 1960s, researcher James McConnell conducted unusual experiments on flatworms called: Planaria\r\nHe trained the worms to react fearfully to light by pairing light with mild electric shocks. Eventually, the worms “learned” the response.\r\n\r\nThen came the controversial part.\r\nThe trained worms were fed to untrained worms.\r\nMcConnell claimed that the new worms learned the behavior faster than normal, as if some form of memory had been biologically transferred.\r\nThe scientific community was divided:\r\nSome believed memory-related molecules might exist.\r\nOthers argued the experiments were inconsistent and difficult to reproduce reliably.\r\n\r\nWhere Is Memory Stored? the traditional explanation says memories are stored through:\r\nstrengthened neural connections,\r\nand changes in brain circuitry.\r\n\r\nThis concept is known as:\r\nSynaptic Plasticity\r\nBut newer research has raised another possibility:\r\nWhat if memories also leave biological traces inside cells themselves?\r\nThis is where scientists became interested in:\r\nRNA — the molecule responsible for carrying cellular instructions.\r\n\r\nThe Sea Creature Study ,In 2018, researchers from University of California, Los Angeles studied a sea slug called: Aplysia\r\n\r\nThis animal is commonly used in neuroscience because of its relatively simple nervous system.\r\nScientists extracted RNA from trained sea slugs that had learned a defensive reaction, then injected that RNA into untrained slugs.\r\nThe surprising result was that the untrained slugs began showing a similar defensive response, almost as if they had inherited part of the memory.\r\n\r\nHowever, scientists were careful with their conclusions:\r\nThey did not claim that full memories were transferred.\r\n\r\nInstead, the RNA may have transferred:\r\n\r\na biological state,\r\na neural sensitivity,\r\nor cellular changes linked to learning.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy Is This Still Controversial?\r\nBecause human memory is far more complex than simple reflexes.\r\nOur memories involve:\r\nemotions,\r\nawareness,\r\nidentity,\r\nperception,\r\nand consciousness.\r\n\r\nThere is currently no evidence that complete human memories can be transferred from one person to another.\r\n\r\nBut these experiments suggest something fascinating:\r\nlearning may leave biological signatures deeper than we once thought.\r\n\r\nThe Big Question , If memories someday prove to have a transferable biological code, it could completely change our understanding of:\r\nlearning,\r\ntrauma,\r\nneurological diseases,\r\nand even human identity itself.\r\n\r\nThe future question may not be:\r\n“What do you remember?”\r\nbut instead:\r\n“Where did that memory originally come from?”`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n      {\r\n      title: \"\",\r\n      date: \"2026-05-06\",\r\n      photos: [\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/ape1.jpeg\",\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/ape2.jpeg\",\r\n  \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/bw3123/our-treasure@main/pics/ape3.jpeg\"\r\n],\r\n      content: `At first glance, the name “Ngogo Chimpanzee War” sounds almost like a dark joke… but the reality is far more brutal.\r\nCompetition has always been part of survival — a defining trait of living beings. But how far can it go?\r\nIn 2015, in Ngogo within Kibale National Park, western Uganda, a dramatic shift in power ignited what can only be described as a civil war among chimpanzees.\r\nThis is not unprecedented… not unprecedented at all (remember this point ✌\uFE0F).\r\n A massive community of around 200 individuals split into two factions: a western group and a central group.\r\nScientists suggest several possible causes behind this violent division:\r\n* The unusually large group size, which may have exceeded the natural limits for maintaining social bonds\r\n* The loss of key “social bridge” males in 2014, who once connected different subgroups\r\n* A change in leadership, with the rise of a new dominant alpha male\r\n* A respiratory disease outbreak in 2017 that killed important members and destabilized the group\r\nThe conflict has been devastating:\r\n28 individuals confirmed dead — including 19 infants and 9 adult males from the central group.\r\nAround 14 more males disappeared, and are also believed to have been killed.\r\nCurrently, the balance seems to favor the western faction — driven by higher aggression, precise planning, and calculated strategies — suggesting they may soon eliminate the rival group’s males entirely.\r\n\r\nEvents like this are incredibly rare, estimated to occur once every 300–500 years. Yet astonishingly, this is the second recorded case in just the past 50 years (✌\uFE0F).\r\nThe first was in 1974 — the famous “Gombe Chimpanzee War,” also known as the Four-Year War — where chimpanzees split into two groups. The northern faction used calculated tactics and strategic ambushes to systematically eliminate the rival males.where chimpanzees split into two groups: one remained in the north, while the other — made up of 7 males, along with females and infants — moved toward the central territory.\r\nThe northern faction proved highly tactical, using coordinated strategies and ambushes to systematically eliminate the rival males.\r\n\r\nWhile competition in nature is normal, events like these have completely reshaped how we see chimpanzees. Once viewed as peaceful and gentle creatures, they reveal a darker side — one driven by organized violence, strategy, and something that eerily resembles political conflict.\r\nNature is not always as innocent as it seems.`\r\n    },\r\n\r\n  ]\r\n};\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// STARS\r\n// ====================================================\r\n(function() {\r\n  const c = document.getElementById('stars');\r\n  for (let i = 0; i < 120; i++) {\r\n    const s = document.createElement('div');\r\n    s.className = 'star';\r\n    s.style.cssText = `left:${Math.random()*100}%;top:${Math.random()*100}%;opacity:${Math.random()*0.7+0.1};--dur:${2+Math.random()*4}s;--delay:-${Math.random()*5}s;width:${Math.random()<0.7?1:2}px;height:${Math.random()<0.7?1:2}px`;\r\n    c.appendChild(s);\r\n  }\r\n})();\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// PAGE SWITCH\r\n// ====================================================\r\nfunction showPage(name) {\r\n  document.querySelectorAll('.page').forEach(p => p.classList.remove('active'));\r\n  document.getElementById('page-' + name).classList.add('active');\r\n\r\n  const nav = document.getElementById('main-nav');\r\n  const tabMain = document.getElementById('tab-main');\r\n  const tabWed = document.getElementById('tab-wed');\r\n  const tabTasks = document.getElementById('tab-tasks');\r\n  const tabMovies = document.getElementById('tab-movies');\r\n\r\n  tabMain.className = 'nav-tab';\r\n  tabWed.className = 'nav-tab';\r\n  tabTasks.className = 'nav-tab';\r\n  tabMovies.className = 'nav-tab';\r\n\r\n  if (name === 'wednesday') {\r\n    nav.classList.add('wed-mode');\r\n    tabWed.className = 'nav-tab active-wed';\r\n  }\r\n  else if (name === 'main') {\r\n    nav.classList.remove('wed-mode');\r\n    tabMain.className = 'nav-tab active-main';\r\n  }\r\n    else if (name === 'tasks') {\r\n\r\n      if (authInProgress) return;\r\n\r\n      nav.classList.remove('wed-mode');\r\n      tabTasks.className = 'nav-tab active-main';\r\n\r\n      if (!isUnlocked(\"tasksUnlockedUntil\")) {\r\n        const ok = checkTasksPassword();\r\n        if (!ok) return;\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      ensureTasksLoaded();\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\n    else if (name === 'movies') {\r\n\r\n      if (authInProgress) return;\r\n\r\n      nav.classList.remove('wed-mode');\r\n      tabMovies.className = 'nav-tab active-main';\r\n\r\n      if (!isUnlocked(\"moviesUnlockedUntil\")) {\r\n        const ok = checkMoviesPassword();\r\n        if (!ok) return;\r\n      }\r\n\r\n      setTimeout(() => ensureMoviesLoaded(), 0);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n  window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });\r\n}\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// DONT KNOW\r\n// ====================================================\r\nfunction wrapMixedText(text) {\r\n  return text\r\n    .split('\\n')\r\n    .map(line => {\r\n      const isArabic = /[\\u0600-\\u06FF]/.test(line);\r\n      const dir = isArabic ? 'rtl' : 'ltr';\r\n      return `<div dir=\"${dir}\" style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">${line}</div>`;\r\n    })\r\n    .join('');\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// RENDER POSTS\r\n// ====================================================\r\nfunction formatDate(d) {\r\n  const months = ['Jan','Feb','Mar','Apr','May','Jun','Jul','Aug','Sep','Oct','Nov','Dec'];\r\n  const [y, m, day] = d.split('-');\r\n  return `${months[+m-1]} ${+day}, ${y}`;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction renderPosts(posts, containerId, isWed) {\r\n  const container = document.getElementById(containerId);\r\n  const line = container.querySelector('.timeline-line');\r\n  container.innerHTML = '';\r\n  if (line) container.appendChild(line);\r\n\r\n  if (posts.length === 0) {\r\n    const el = document.createElement('div');\r\n    el.className = 'no-posts';\r\n    el.textContent = 'No posts found';\r\n    container.appendChild(el);\r\n    return;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  posts.forEach((post, i) => {\r\n    const row = document.createElement('div');\r\n    row.className = 'post-row';\r\n\r\n    const dot = document.createElement('div');\r\n    dot.className = 'timeline-dot';\r\n    row.appendChild(dot);\r\n\r\n    const card = document.createElement('div');\r\n    card.className = 'post-card' + (isWed ? ' wed-card' : '');\r\n    card.onclick = () => openModal(post, isWed);\r\n\r\n    if (post.photos && post.photos.length) {\r\n      card.innerHTML += `\r\n        <div class=\"card-img\">\r\n          <img src=\"${post.photos[0]}\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" />\r\n          <div class=\"card-img-overlay\"></div>\r\n          ${post.photos.length > 1 ? `<span class=\"${isWed ? 'photo-count wed-photo-count' : 'photo-count'}\">\r\n            <svg width=\"11\" height=\"11\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8.5\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"m21 15-5-5L5 21\"/></svg>\r\n            ${post.photos.length}\r\n          </span>` : ''}\r\n        </div>`;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    card.innerHTML += `\r\n      <div class=\"card-body\">\r\n        <div class=\"card-date\">\r\n          <svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18\"/></svg>\r\n          ${formatDate(post.date)}\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div class=\"card-title\">${post.title}</div>\r\n        <div class=\"card-excerpt\">${post.content.slice(0, 200)}...</div>\r\n      </div>`;\r\n\r\n    row.appendChild(card);\r\n    container.appendChild(row);\r\n\r\n    // Intersection observer for stagger\r\n    setTimeout(() => {\r\n      const obs = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {\r\n        entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('visible'); obs.disconnect(); } });\r\n      }, { threshold: 0.1 });\r\n      obs.observe(row);\r\n    }, i * 80);\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// FILTER\r\n// ====================================================\r\nlet filtered = { main: [...POSTS.main], wed: [...POSTS.wednesday] };\r\n\r\nfunction filterPosts(type) {\r\n  const isWed = type === 'wed';\r\n  const searchVal = document.getElementById(type + '-search-input').value.toLowerCase();\r\n  const from = document.getElementById(type + '-date-from').value;\r\n  const to = document.getElementById(type + '-date-to').value;\r\n\r\n  const clearBtn = document.getElementById(type + '-clear');\r\n  clearBtn.style.display = searchVal ? 'block' : 'none';\r\n\r\n  const source = isWed ? POSTS.wednesday : POSTS.main;\r\n  filtered[type] = source.filter(p => {\r\n    if (searchVal && !p.title.toLowerCase().includes(searchVal) && !p.content.toLowerCase().includes(searchVal)) return false;\r\n    if (from && p.date < from) return false;\r\n    if (to && p.date > to) return false;\r\n    return true;\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  renderPosts(filtered[type], isWed ? 'timeline-wed' : 'timeline-main', isWed);\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction clearSearch(type) {\r\n  document.getElementById(type + '-search-input').value = '';\r\n  filterPosts(type);\r\n}\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// MODAL & CAROUSEL\r\n// ====================================================\r\nlet carouselIdx = 0;\r\nlet carouselPhotos = [];\r\nlet isWedModal = false;\r\n\r\nfunction openModal(post, isWed) {\r\n  isWedModal = isWed;\r\n  const modal = document.getElementById('modal-box');\r\n  const closeBtn = document.getElementById('modal-close-btn');\r\n  modal.className = 'modal' + (isWed ? ' wed-modal' : '');\r\n  closeBtn.className = 'modal-close' + (isWed ? ' wed-modal-close' : '');\r\n\r\n  document.getElementById('modal-date').innerHTML = `\r\n    <svg width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18\"/></svg>\r\n    ${formatDate(post.date)}`;\r\n  document.getElementById('modal-title').textContent = post.title;\r\n  document.getElementById('modal-content').innerHTML = wrapMixedText(post.content);\r\n\r\n  // Carousel\r\n  carouselPhotos = post.photos || [];\r\n  carouselIdx = 0;\r\n  buildCarousel(isWed);\r\n\r\n  document.getElementById('modal').classList.add('open');\r\n  document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction buildCarousel(isWed) {\r\n  const track = document.getElementById('carousel-track');\r\n  const dots = document.getElementById('carousel-dots');\r\n  const prev = document.getElementById('carousel-prev');\r\n  const next = document.getElementById('carousel-next');\r\n\r\n  prev.className = 'carousel-btn prev' + (isWed ? ' wed-carousel-btn' : '');\r\n  next.className = 'carousel-btn next' + (isWed ? ' wed-carousel-btn' : '');\r\n\r\n\ttrack.innerHTML = carouselPhotos.map(p => `\r\n\t  <div class=\"carousel-slide\">\r\n\t\t${\r\n\t\t  p.endsWith('.mp4')\r\n\t\t  ? `\r\n\t\t\t<video\r\n\t\t\t  controls\r\n\t\t\t  playsinline\r\n\t\t\t  style=\"width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;background:#000;\"\r\n\t\t\t>\r\n\t\t\t  <source src=\"${p}\" type=\"video/mp4\">\r\n\t\t\t</video>\r\n\t\t  `\r\n\t\t  : `<img src=\"${p}\" alt=\"\" />`\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t  </div>\r\n\t`).join('');\r\n\r\n  dots.innerHTML = carouselPhotos.map((_, i) => `\r\n    <button class=\"carousel-dot${isWed?' wed-carousel-dot':''}${i===0?' active':''}\" onclick=\"carouselGo(${i})\"></button>\r\n  `).join('');\r\n\r\n  prev.style.display = carouselPhotos.length > 1 ? 'flex' : 'none';\r\n  next.style.display = carouselPhotos.length > 1 ? 'flex' : 'none';\r\n  dots.style.display = carouselPhotos.length > 1 ? 'flex' : 'none';\r\n\r\n  document.getElementById('modal-carousel').style.display = carouselPhotos.length ? 'block' : 'none';\r\n  updateCarousel();\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction updateCarousel() {\r\n  document.getElementById('carousel-track').style.transform = `translateX(-${carouselIdx * 100}%)`;\r\n  document.querySelectorAll('.carousel-dot').forEach((d, i) => {\r\n    d.classList.toggle('active', i === carouselIdx);\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction carouselPrev() { carouselIdx = (carouselIdx - 1 + carouselPhotos.length) % carouselPhotos.length; updateCarousel(); }\r\nfunction carouselNext() { carouselIdx = (carouselIdx + 1) % carouselPhotos.length; updateCarousel(); }\r\nfunction carouselGo(i) { carouselIdx = i; updateCarousel(); }\r\n\r\nfunction closeModal(e) {\r\n  if (e && e.target !== document.getElementById('modal') && !e.target.classList.contains('modal-close')) return;\r\n  document.getElementById('modal').classList.remove('open');\r\n  document.body.style.overflow = '';\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Keyboard nav\r\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', e => {\r\n  if (!document.getElementById('modal').classList.contains('open')) return;\r\n  if (e.key === 'Escape') closeModal({target: document.getElementById('modal')});\r\n  if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') carouselPrev();\r\n  if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') carouselNext();\r\n});\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// COUNTDOWN\r\n// ====================================================\r\nfunction getNextWed() {\r\n  const now = new Date();\r\n  const target = new Date(now);\r\n  target.setHours(12, 0, 0, 0);\r\n  const day = now.getDay();\r\n  let diff = (3 - day + 7) % 7;\r\n  if (diff === 0 && now >= target) diff = 7;\r\n  target.setDate(target.getDate() + diff);\r\n  return target;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction pad(n) { return String(n).padStart(2, '0'); }\r\n\r\nfunction updateCountdown() {\r\n  const diff = Math.max(0, getNextWed() - new Date());\r\n  const d = Math.floor(diff / 86400000);\r\n  const h = Math.floor((diff % 86400000) / 3600000);\r\n  const m = Math.floor((diff % 3600000) / 60000);\r\n  const s = Math.floor((diff % 60000) / 1000);\r\n  const ids = ['cd-days','cd-hours','cd-mins','cd-secs'];\r\n  const vals = [d, h, m, s];\r\n  ids.forEach((id, i) => {\r\n    const el = document.getElementById(id);\r\n    const newVal = pad(vals[i]);\r\n    if (el.textContent !== newVal) {\r\n      el.style.animation = 'none';\r\n      el.offsetHeight; // reflow\r\n      el.style.animation = '';\r\n      el.textContent = newVal;\r\n    }\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\nsetInterval(updateCountdown, 1000);\r\nupdateCountdown();\r\n\r\n// ====================================================\r\n// INIT\r\n// ====================================================\r\nrenderPosts(POSTS.main, 'timeline-main', false);\r\nrenderPosts(POSTS.wednesday, 'timeline-wed', true);\r\n\r\n\r\nupdateToggleUI('task', 'all');\r\nupdateToggleUI('movie', 'all');\r\n\r\n//\r\n//function checkMoviesPassword() {\r\n//  const pw = prompt(\"Enter password for Movies:\");\r\n//\r\n//  if (!pw) return false;\r\n//\r\n//  if (pw === \"batrnan\") {\r\n//    const expiry = Date.now() + 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\r\n//    localStorage.setItem(\"moviesUnlockedUntil\", expiry);\r\n//\r\n//    ensureMoviesLoaded();\r\n//    showPage('movies'); // ✅ ADD THIS\r\n//  } else {\r\n//    alert(\"Wrong password ❌\");\r\n//    return false;\r\n//  }\r\n//}\r\nlet pendingUnlock = null;\r\n\r\nfunction openPasswordModal(type) {\r\n  pendingUnlock = type;\r\n\r\n  document.getElementById(\"password-title\").textContent =\r\n    type === \"movies\" ? \"Unlock Movies\" : \"Unlock Tasks\";\r\n\r\n  document.getElementById(\"password-input\").value = \"\";\r\n  document.getElementById(\"password-modal\").classList.remove(\"hidden\");\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction closePasswordModal() {\r\n  document.getElementById(\"password-modal\").classList.add(\"hidden\");\r\n  pendingUnlock = null;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction submitPassword() {\r\n  const pw = document.getElementById(\"password-input\").value;\r\n\r\n  if (!pw) return;\r\n\r\n  if (pw === \"batrnan\") {\r\n    const expiry = Date.now() + 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\r\n\r\n    if (pendingUnlock === \"movies\") {\r\n      localStorage.setItem(\"moviesUnlockedUntil\", expiry);\r\n      ensureMoviesLoaded();\r\n      showPage(\"movies\");\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    if (pendingUnlock === \"tasks\") {\r\n      localStorage.setItem(\"tasksUnlockedUntil\", expiry);\r\n      ensureTasksLoaded();\r\n      showPage(\"tasks\");\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    closePasswordModal();\r\n  } else {\r\n    alert(\"Wrong password ❌\");\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\n//\r\n//function checkTasksPassword() {\r\n//  const pw = prompt(\"Enter password for Tasks:\");\r\n//\r\n//  if (!pw) return false;\r\n//\r\n//  if (pw === \"batrnan\") {\r\n//    const expiry = Date.now() + 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\r\n//    localStorage.setItem(\"tasksUnlockedUntil\", expiry);\r\n//\r\n//    ensureTasksLoaded();\r\n//    showPage('tasks'); // ✅ ADD THIS\r\n//  } else {\r\n//    alert(\"Wrong password ❌\");\r\n//    return false;\r\n//  }\r\n//}\r\n//\r\n\r\n\r\n\t/* ONE PIECE ROTATOR */\r\n\r\nconst onePieceSlides =\r\n  document.querySelectorAll(\".onepiece-slide\");\r\n\r\nlet onePieceIndex = 0;\r\n\r\nsetInterval(() => {\r\n\r\n  onePieceSlides[onePieceIndex]\r\n    .classList.remove(\"active\");\r\n\r\n  onePieceIndex =\r\n    (onePieceIndex + 1) % onePieceSlides.length;\r\n\r\n  onePieceSlides[onePieceIndex]\r\n    .classList.add(\"active\");\r\n\r\n}, 4000);\r\n\r\n\r\nfunction setTaskFilter(type) {\r\n  taskFilter = type;\r\n  updateToggleUI('task', type);\r\n  renderTasks();\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction setMovieFilter(type) {\r\n  movieFilter = type;\r\n  updateToggleUI('movie', type);\r\n  renderMovies();\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction updateToggleUI(type, value) {\r\n  const map = {\r\n    task: 'task-toggle',\r\n    movie: 'movie-toggle'\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  const container = document.getElementById(map[type]);\r\n  if (!container) return;\r\n\r\n  container.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(btn => {\r\n    btn.classList.remove('active');\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  if (value === 'all') container.children[0].classList.add('active');\r\n  if (value === 'pending') container.children[1].classList.add('active');\r\n  if (value === 'done') container.children[2].classList.add('active');\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\nfunction chooseRandomMovie() {\r\n  const unwatched = movies.filter(m => !m.watched);\r\n\r\n  if (unwatched.length === 0) {\r\n    const el = document.getElementById(\"movie-suggestion\");\r\n    el.textContent = \"\uD83C\uDF89 No unwatched movies!\";\r\n    return;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const random = unwatched[Math.floor(Math.random() * unwatched.length)];\r\n\r\n  const el = document.getElementById(\"movie-suggestion\");\r\n\r\n  el.style.transform = \"scale(0.95)\";\r\n  el.style.opacity = \"0.5\";\r\n\r\n  setTimeout(() => {\r\n    el.textContent = \"\uD83C\uDFAC Watch next: \" + random.title;\r\n\r\n    el.style.transform = \"scale(1)\";\r\n    el.style.opacity = \"1\";\r\n  }, 120);\r\n}\r\n\r\n\r\nfunction isUnlocked(key) {\r\n  const value = localStorage.getItem(key);\r\n  if (!value) return false;\r\n\r\n  const expiry = Number(value);\r\n  return Date.now() < expiry;\r\n}\r\n
